.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Things related to animation\&. 

See \fBParticle effects\fP for lightweight particles, point emitters and nested trails\&.

.PP
Authored eventline notifications are described in \fBAuthored Spriter triggers\fP and delivered with the \fBpdg::SpriteTriggerEvent\fP payload\&. 
.SH "Class Documentation"
.PP 
.SH "class pdg::IAnimationHelper"
.PP 
helper for add-on or complex motion during animation 


.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
\fBAPI Stability: 2 — Evolving\fP\&. This API is implemented and supported, but its contract is still settling\&. Compatibility is preserved where practical; breaking changes are documented in release notes\&. See \fBAPI stability\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
Implement this interface to do extra animation stuff for a specific \fBAnimated\fP object then add by calling the object's addAnimationHelper() method\&. You can have multiple Animation Helpers attached to the same object\&. Your helper will then be called every time movement for the object is calculated\&.

.PP
To create a helper:

.PP
.PP
.nf
const myHelper = new pdg\&.IAnimationHelper(function(what, deltaSeconds) {
                console\&.log("in my animation helper for " + what + " after " + deltaSeconds + " seconds" );
                return true;  // not done, keep helping
});
myAnimatedObj\&.addAnimationHelper(myHelper);
.fi
.PP

.PP
For a helper with its own methods or state, declare a JavaScript class that extends \fR\fBpdg\&.IAnimationHelper\fP\fP\&. The native interface takes a callback in its constructor; forward that callback to your \fRanimate()\fP method through \fRsuper()\fP:

.PP
.PP
.nf
class MyAnimationHelperClass extends pdg\&.IAnimationHelper {
    constructor() {
        super(function(what, deltaSeconds) {
            return this\&.animate(what, deltaSeconds);
        });
    }

    animate(what, deltaSeconds) {
        console\&.log("Animation step:", deltaSeconds, "seconds");
        return false; // finished; remove this helper from the object
    }
}

myAnimatedObj\&.addAnimationHelper(new MyAnimationHelperClass());
.fi
.PP
.SS "Your Custom Function:"
As you can see from the examples above, your Animation Helper function (or animate() method) will be called with two parameters, and return a boolean: 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwhat\fP the \fBAnimated\fP object that is being animated 
.br
\fIdeltaSeconds\fP the elapsed time in floating-point seconds since the last time this object's movement was calculated 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
\fBtrue\fP if the helper should continue to be called; or \fBfalse\fP if it is done and should be removed from this \fBAnimated\fP object\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SH "struct pdg::SpriteAnimateEvent"
.PP 
a Sprite did some animation (\fIOptional\fP) 

A Sprite will generate one of these events when it completes an animation including fades (opacity animations), and moving on/offscreen or outside of the layer\&.

.PP
For frame based animations -- that is, calls to \fBpdg\&.Sprite\&.startFrameAnimation()\fP -- if it reaches the last frame and is not set to loop, action will be \fBpdg\&.action_AnimationEnd\fP\&. For looping animations \fBpdg\&.action_AnimationLoop\fP will be received each time the animation completes and starts over with the first frame\&.

.PP
When a Spriter animation blend started by \fBpdg::Sprite::blendToAnimation()\fP or \fBpdg::Sprite::transitionToAnimation()\fP completes, action is \fBpdg::action_AnimationBlendComplete\fP\&.

.PP
Authored Spriter triggers are delivered as \fBpdg::eventType_SpriteTriggerEvent\fP with a \fBpdg::SpriteTriggerEvent\fP payload\&. Subscribe to that event type for triggers\&.

.PP
For fades, one of three action types are possible: \fBpdg\&.action_FadeComplete\fP for calls to \fBpdg\&.Sprite\&.fadeTo()\fP, \fBpdg\&.action_FadeInComplete\fP for calls to \fBpdg\&.Sprite\&.fadeIn()\fP, and \fBpdg\&.action_FadeOutComplete\fP for calls to \fBpdg\&.Sprite\&.fadeOut()\fP\&.

.PP
When a Sprite has setWantsOffscreenEvents(true), \fBpdg\&.action_Offscreen\fP and \fBpdg\&.action_Onscreen\fP events will be generated for that sprite whenever it enters or departs the visible area of the port the layer is being rendered into\&.

.PP
When a Sprite has setWantsCollideWallEvents(true), \fBpdg\&.action_ExitLayer\fP events will be generated for that sprite whenever it moves completely outside the boundaries of the layer\&. (It will also get a \fBSpriteCollideEvent\fP when it hits the boundary)\&. 
.PP
.nf
{
    emitter: {},       // the emitter that generated this event
    eventType: 17,     // the event type (eventType_SpriteAnimate)
    action: 0,         // what happened (action_AnimationEnd/Loop or action_Fade/In/OutComplete)
    actingSprite: {},  // the Sprite that was animating
    inLayer: {}        // the SpriteLayer that contains the Sprite
}

.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Spriter eventline notifications require pdg::Sprite::enableSpriterEvents(true)\&. See \fBAuthored Spriter triggers\fP for crossing, looping, seek, and transition rules\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
